overfit": "pass — 0 new parameters; L1/L2 designs cite only pre-existing engine constants (`0.005` threshold at `simulate_holistic_nav.py:913`, `etf_frac=0.70` from `PARK_STATES`, `_etf_day_cap`, FIFO, `×0.99`) already embedded in the pinned backtest, not re-tuned.", "capacity_adv_realism": "fail — read `_etf_day_cap()` at `simulate_holistic_nav.py:440-446`: it is `etf_liquidity_pct × etf_adv_lookup.get(today)`, i.e. calibrated to **E1VFVN30 ETF's own ADV**, not to the ADV of the 30 discrete equities in the live [REDACTED]V basket. Section B2/B4 proposes reusing this exact cap verbatim as the live per-session trim ceiling ('không đặt trần %/phiên mới... `_etf_day_cap` đã có sẵn') while simultaneously acknowledging (B4) that live PARK is '30 mã riêng lẻ' vs the engine's pooled-ETF abstraction — but never reconciles that the liquidity ceiling itself, not just the trim ORDER, was pooled-ETF-shaped. Applying an ETF-ADV-sized VND cap to trims spread across up to 30 individual (some potentially illiquid) value names risks breaching per-name %ADV even while staying under the aggregate cap.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "pass — verified the '6/13 years C beats A' sub-claim by hand from the raw annual tables: C > A in exactly 2016, 2017, 2019, 2020, 2022, 2025 (6 years) — exact match to the doc's named years. `w_lag_current=0.495`/`alloc_note='as of [REDACTED]'`/`band_breach=false`/`n_park=30`/`park_rebal_date=2026-05-05`/`etf_park_frac=0.7` all reproduced byte-for-byte from `data/golive_v23_status.json`. `deferred_total_with_fee_vnd=171,096,626`, `available_cash_vnd=4,821,143`, `orders=[]` and the literal deferred_reason text reproduced from `data/trade_plans/plan_[REDACTED]_[REDACTED].json`. `totalCash=14,596,244` reproduced from `dnse_raw_[REDACTED]03.jsonl`. Mechanism claims (allocator is post-hoc scalar accounting, not order-generating; DT5G is untouched by this whole topic) are consistent with code."}, "independent_recompute": "Recomputed IS/OOS geometric CAGR from the raw